      <title>Squeak 2.27.0</title>
      <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:00:52 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22700</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.27.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>New setting in Account: "Keep recent chats in Squeak's cloud (encrypted)", on by default once you are signed in. Your iPhone and browser can then open your last 30 days of chats while this Mac sleeps, or on a new device. The copy is sealed with your key, so Squeak can't read it; turning the setting off deletes it.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.26.4</h4><ul><li>A chat interrupted by a restart now closes the right turn; Markdown preview only shows images inside the workspace.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.26.3</h4><ul><li>Chat polish: earlier turns no longer redraw when only the newest one changes, long commands shorten in the middle, durations keep their width as they tick, long command output stops at 12 lines with Show all, and steps read their duration and open state to VoiceOver.</li><li>A reply being written re-parses only its last block, so long replies stay smooth as they stream; teammates' names stay on one line and read "From ...".</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
